  "content": {
    "id": "p52-g108-110",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Show that for real values of $k\\ne0$, the following equations have no real roots.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p52-g108-110-a",
        "type": "question",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2-2kx+3k^2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=-8k^2<0$ for $k\\ne0$, so there are no real roots.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-2k)^2-4(1)(3k^2)\\\\\\Delta&=4k^2-12k^2\\\\\\Delta&=-8k^2<0\\qquad(k\\ne0).\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence the equation has no real roots.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-g108-110-b",
        "type": "question",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2+2x+1+k^2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=-4k^2<0$ for $k\\ne0$, so there are no real roots.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=2^2-4(1)(1+k^2)\\\\\\Delta&=4-4-4k^2\\\\\\Delta&=-4k^2<0\\qquad(k\\ne0).\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence the equation has no real roots.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p52-g108-110-c",
        "type": "question",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^2+2kx+2k^2+k+1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p52-g108-110-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\Delta=-4\\left[\\left(k+\\frac12\\right)^2+\\frac34\\right]<0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", so there are no real roots.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p52-g108-110-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Complete the square in the discriminant; the bracket is positive for every real ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(2k)^2-4(1)(2k^2+k+1)\\\\\\Delta&=-4(k^2+k+1)\\\\\\Delta&=-4\\left[\\left(k+\\frac12\\right)^2+\\frac34\\right]<0.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe square is nonnegative, so the bracket is positive for every real $k$. Hence the equation has no real roots for the stated $k\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
